NOTE ON MODEL WEIGHTS

This MIT license covers the CODE IN THIS REPOSITORY ONLY.

The Liquid AI LFM2.5 base weights are licensed separately under the
LFM Open License v1.0, which is NOT MIT and NOT OSI-approved. It is based on
Apache 2.0 but adds a commercial-use limitation: free commercial use is
restricted to legal entities with under USD 10,000,000 in annual revenue.
Qualified non-profits are exempt from that threshold for non-commercial or
research use.

Consequences for this project:
  - Our training/inference/eval code: MIT (this file).
  - Trained weights derived from LFM2.5: LFM Open License v1.0. They are NOT
    MIT-licensed, and redistributing them requires including the LFM license,
    retaining attribution notices, and marking modified files.
  - We do not relicense the base weights. The LFM license has no copyleft
    requirement, so you may keep fine-tuned weights proprietary, but they stay
    under the LFM terms.

See https://www.liquid.ai/lfm-open-license-v1.0 for the authoritative text and
https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/LFM2.5-350M/blob/main/LICENSE for the copy that
ships with the weights.

Jeb-Omni-Nano is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
sponsored by, or derived from TypeSafe AI or its Jev model. No Jev output was
used in training.
